; fakereal_full.def — exports of the fake real DLL (Win32 harness only).
; The 3 stdcall names MUST match what gshim.c resolves
; ("_grBufferSwap@4" etc.); fakereal_counts is the harness-only
; interrogation export. Missing-one-export variants are generated by
; build-harness.sh (this file minus one line each), so the fake keeps
; its code but loses the export — GetProcAddress then fails exactly
; like a real DLL lacking that symbol.
; MINGW-32 LINK RULE (same latent defect as gshim.def, 2026-10-11):
; explicit-alias form "decorated"=internal only (internal WITHOUT the
; leading underscore) — bare decorated lines fail the current MinGW-32
; link. Variant generation (grep -vF '_gr...@N') still matches, since
; the decorated name stays on its own line.
LIBRARY glide2x_gex_real
EXPORTS
    "_grBufferSwap@4"=grBufferSwap@4
    "_grBufferNumPending@0"=grBufferNumPending@0
    "_grGlideShutdown@0"=grGlideShutdown@0
    "_fakereal_counts@16"=fakereal_counts@16
